<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Weah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as George Manneh Weah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Weah is a Liberian footballer and politician. A striker for clubs including Monaco, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Saint-Germain and AC <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, he was named FIFA World Player of the Year and won the Ballon d'Or in 1995, the first African to do so. He was president of Liberia from 2018 to 2024 and accepted defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-boakai">Joseph Boakai</a> in the 2023 election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-weah.jpg" alt="George Weah" width="301" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Department of State Africa U.S.-Africa Leaders Summit: Photos and Videos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clar_Weah,_George_Weah,_Joe_Biden,_Jill_Biden_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
